{"title":"SCC Generated CKLB at: 2026-09-05T13:09:58","id":"88E6E310-6BF8-1014-A4BD-999496D5EB52","cklb_version":"1.0","stigs":[{"stig_name":"Microsoft Edge Security Technical Implementation Guide","uuid":"88DD52C8-6BF8-1014-BE64-C3AC2D3D7E13","size":61,"reference_identifier":"5280","classification":"UNCLASSIFIED","stig_id":"MS_Edge_STIG","rules":[{"potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-235719","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-235719","fix_text":"Set the policy value for \"Computer Configuration/Administrative Templates/Microsoft Edge/Proxy server/Proxy Settings\" to \"Enabled\" and define a value for \"ProxyMode\".\n\n\"ProxyMode\" must be defined and set to one of the following: \"direct\", \"system\", \"auto_detect\", \"fixed_servers\", or \"pac_script\".\n\nConsult Microsoft documentation for proper configuration of the text string required to define the \"Proxy Settings\" value.\n\nExample:  {\"ProxyMode\": \"fixed_servers\", \"ProxyServer\": \"127.0.0.1:8080\"}\n\n\"ProxyPacUrl\", \"ProxyServer\", or \"ProxyBypassList\" are optional.","status":"open","uuid":"88E09A62-6BF8-1014-A861-A1641D5DD5A6","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Edge_V2R5_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV15-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.edge:def:235719"},"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:09:53\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   false (User control of proxy settings must be disabled.)\nResult Analysis         :        HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Edge\\ProxySettings\\value = 'ADD YOUR PROXY CONFIGURATIONS HERE' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to '\"ProxyMode\":(\\s+)?(\"direct\"|\"system\"|\"auto_detect\"|\"fixed_servers\"|\"pac_script\")' \n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.edge:tst:23571901 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : User control of proxy settings must be disabled.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.edge:obj:23571901 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : ProxySettings\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Edge'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'ProxySettings'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.edge:ste:23571901 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : 'ProxyMode' must be defined and set to one of the following: 'direct', 'system', 'auto_detect', 'fixed_servers', or 'pac_script'.\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'name' must be equal to 'ProxySettings'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must match the pattern '\"ProxyMode\":(\\s+)?(\"direct\"|\"system\"|\"auto_detect\"|\"fixed_servers\"|\"pac_script\")'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Edge'\n                        : name equals 'ProxySettings'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_sz'\n                        : value equals 'ADD YOUR PROXY CONFIGURATIONS HERE'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n\nResult Analysis         : HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Edge\\ProxySettings\\value = 'ADD YOUR PROXY CONFIGURATIONS HERE' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to '\"ProxyMode\":(\\s+)?(\"direct\"|\"system\"|\"auto_detect\"|\"fixed_servers\"|\"pac_script\")' \n","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"User control of proxy settings must be disabled.","discussion":"This action configures the proxy settings for Microsoft Edge.\n\nIf this policy is enabled, Microsoft Edge ignores all proxy-related options specified from the command line.\n\nIf this policy is not configured, users can choose their own proxy settings.\n\nThis policy overrides the following individual policies:\n- ProxyMode.\n- ProxyPacUrl. \n- ProxyServer. \n- ProxyBypassList.\n\nSetting the ProxySettings policy accepts the following fields:\n- ProxyMode, which allows for the proxy server used by Microsoft Edge to be specified and prevents users from changing proxy settings.\n- ProxyPacUrl, a URL to a proxy .pac file.\n- ProxyServer, a URL for the proxy server.\n- ProxyBypassList, a list of proxy hosts that Microsoft Edge bypasses.\n\nFor ProxyMode, the following values have the noted impact:\n- direct, a proxy is never used and all other fields are ignored.\n- system, the system's proxy is used and all other fields are ignored.\n- auto_detect, all other fields are ignored.\n- fixed_servers, the ProxyServer and ProxyBypassList fields are used.\n- pac_script, the ProxyPacUrl and ProxyBypassList fields are used.","mitigations":"","stig_uuid":"88DD52C8-6BF8-1014-BE64-C3AC2D3D7E13","rule_version":"EDGE-00-000001","group_title":"SRG-APP-000039","severity":"low","ccis":["CCI-001414"],"ia_controls":"","check_content":"The policy value for \"Computer Configuration/Administrative Templates/Microsoft Edge/Proxy server/Proxy Settings\" must be \"Enabled\", and have a \"Proxy Settings\" value defined for \"ProxyMode\".\n\n\"ProxyMode\" must be defined and set to one of the following: \"direct\", \"system\", \"auto_detect\", \"fixed_servers\", or \"pac_script\".\n\nConsult Microsoft documentation for proper configuration of the text string required to define the \"Proxy Settings\" value.\n\nExample:  {\"ProxyMode\": \"fixed_servers\", \"ProxyServer\": \"123.123.123.123:8080\"}\n\nValues for \"ProxyPacUrl\", \"ProxyServer\", or \"ProxyBypassList\" are optional.\n\nUse the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key:\nHKLM\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Edge\n\nIf the REG_SZ value for \"ProxySettings\" does not have \"ProxyMode\" configured, this is a finding.","rule_id_src":"SV-235719r1156558_rule","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-235719r1156558","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","reference_identifier":"5280","third_party_tools":"","responsibility":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000039","id":"V-235719"}},{"legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-235720","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-235720","fix_text":"Set the policy value for \"Computer Configuration/Administrative Templates/Microsoft Edge/SmartScreen settings/Prevent bypassing Microsoft Defender SmartScreen prompts for sites\" to \"Enabled\".","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.edge:def:100","href":"U_MS_Edge_V2R5_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV15-oval.xml"},"uuid":"88E0B48D-6BF8-1014-B02C-A0435F825CBE","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:09:53\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Enable the setting 'Prevent bypassing Microsoft Defender SmartScreen prompts for sites')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.edge:tst:10000 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Enable the setting 'Prevent bypassing Microsoft Defender SmartScreen prompts for sites'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.edge:obj:10000 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Edge'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'PreventSmartScreenPromptOverride'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.edge:ste:11 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Reg_Dword type and value equals 1\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Edge'\n                        : name equals 'PreventSmartScreenPromptOverride'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","mitigations":"","discussion":"This policy setting allows a decision to be made on whether users can override the Microsoft Defender SmartScreen warnings about potentially malicious websites.\n\nIf this setting is enabled, users cannot ignore Microsoft Defender SmartScreen warnings, and are blocked from continuing to the site.\n\nIf this setting is disabled or not configured, users can ignore Microsoft Defender SmartScreen warnings and continue to the site.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Bypassing Microsoft Defender SmartScreen prompts for sites must be disabled.","stig_uuid":"88DD52C8-6BF8-1014-BE64-C3AC2D3D7E13","rule_version":"EDGE-00-000002","severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-APP-000073","ccis":["CCI-000870"],"rule_id_src":"SV-235720r960852_rule","ia_controls":"","check_content":"The policy value for \"Computer Configuration/Administrative Templates/Microsoft Edge/SmartScreen settings/Prevent bypassing Microsoft Defender SmartScreen prompts for sites\" must be set to \"Enabled\".\n\nUse the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key:\nHKLM\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Edge\n\nIf the value for \"PreventSmartScreenPromptOverride\" is not set to \"REG_DWORD = 1\", this is a finding.\n\nIf this machine is on SIPRNet, this is Not Applicable.","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"rule_id":"SV-235720r960852","mitigation_control":"","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000073","id":"V-235720"},"reference_identifier":"5280","third_party_tools":"","responsibility":""},{"uuid":"88E0BDD2-6BF8-1014-9DF4-C6AED200A1D2","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.edge:def:101","href":"U_MS_Edge_V2R5_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV15-oval.xml"},"status":"not_a_finding","fix_text":"Set the policy value for \"Computer Configuration/Administrative Templates/Microsoft Edge/SmartScreen settings/Prevent bypassing of Microsoft Defender SmartScreen warnings about downloads\" must to \"Enabled\".","group_id":"V-235721","potential_impacts":"","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-235721","stig_uuid":"88DD52C8-6BF8-1014-BE64-C3AC2D3D7E13","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Bypassing of Microsoft Defender SmartScreen warnings about downloads must be disabled.","mitigations":"","discussion":"This policy setting allows a decision to be made on whether users can override Microsoft Defender SmartScreen warnings about unverified downloads.\n\nIf this setting is enabled, users cannot ignore Microsoft Defender SmartScreen warnings, and are prevented from completing the unverified downloads.\n\nIf this policy is disabled or not configured, users can ignore Microsoft Defender SmartScreen warnings and complete unverified downloads.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:09:53\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Enable the setting 'Prevent bypassing Microsoft Defender SmartScreen warnings about downloads')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.edge:tst:10100 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Enable the setting 'Prevent bypassing Microsoft Defender SmartScreen warnings about downloads'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.edge:obj:10100 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Edge'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'PreventSmartScreenPromptOverrideForFiles'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.edge:ste:11 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Reg_Dword type and value equals 1\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Edge'\n                        : name equals 'PreventSmartScreenPromptOverrideForFiles'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","ccis":["CCI-000870"],"severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-APP-000073","rule_version":"EDGE-00-000003","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000073","id":"V-235721"},"third_party_tools":"","reference_identifier":"5280","responsibility":"","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","rule_id":"SV-235721r960852","mitigation_control":"","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","rule_id_src":"SV-235721r960852_rule","ia_controls":"","check_content":"The policy value for \"Computer Configuration/Administrative Templates/Microsoft Edge/SmartScreen settings/Prevent bypassing of Microsoft Defender SmartScreen warnings about downloads\" must be set to \"Enabled\".\n\nUse the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key:\nHKLM\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Edge\n\nIf the value for \"PreventSmartScreenPromptOverrideForFiles\" is not set to \"REG_DWORD = 1\", this is a finding.\n\nIf this machine is on SIPRNet, this is Not Applicable."},{"fix_text":"The policy value for \"Computer Configuration/Administrative Templates/Microsoft Edge/SmartScreen settings/Configure the list of domains for which Microsoft Defender SmartScreen will not trigger warnings\" may be set to \"allow\" for allowlisted domains.","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-235722","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-235722","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Edge_V2R5_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV15-ocil.xml","name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.edge:questionnaire:701"},"uuid":"88E0C599-6BF8-1014-81D5-90D0D149EEC8","status":"not_reviewed","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:09:53\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT III, V-235722, SV-235722r960852, SRG-APP-000073)\n","stig_uuid":"88DD52C8-6BF8-1014-BE64-C3AC2D3D7E13","discussion":"Configure the list of Microsoft Defender SmartScreen trusted domains. This means Microsoft Defender SmartScreen will not check for potentially malicious resources, such as phishing software and other malware, if the source URLs match these domains. The Microsoft Defender SmartScreen download protection service will not check downloads hosted on these domains.\n\nIf this policy is enabled, Microsoft Defender SmartScreen trusts these domains. If the policy is disabled or not set, default Microsoft Defender SmartScreen protection is applied to all resources.","mitigations":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The list of domains for which Microsoft Defender SmartScreen will not trigger warnings must be allowlisted if used.","rule_version":"EDGE-00-000004","ccis":["CCI-000870"],"group_title":"SRG-APP-000073","severity":"low","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-235722r960852","ia_controls":"","check_content":"If this machine is on SIPRNet, this is Not Applicable.\n\nThis requirement for \"SmartScreenAllowListDomains\" is not required; this is optional.\n\nThe policy value for \"Computer Configuration/Administrative Templates/Microsoft Edge/SmartScreen settings/Configure the list of domains for which Microsoft Defender SmartScreen won't trigger warnings\" may be set to \"allow\" for allowlisted domains.\n\nUse the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key:\nHKLM\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Edge\n\nSmartScreenAllowListDomains may be set as follows:\nHKLM\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Edge\\SmartScreenAllowListDomains\\1 = mydomain.com\nHKLM\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Edge\\SmartScreenAllowListDomains\\2 = myagency.mil\n\nIf configured, the list of domains for which Microsoft Defender SmartScreen will not trigger warnings may be allowlisted.","rule_id_src":"SV-235722r960852_rule","responsibility":"","reference_identifier":"5280","third_party_tools":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-235722","title":"SRG-APP-000073"},"weight":"10.0","documentable":"false"},{"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:09:53\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (InPrivate mode is disabled)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.edge:tst:10200 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : InPrivate mode is disabled\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.edge:obj:10200 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Edge'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'InPrivateModeAvailability'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.edge:ste:11 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Reg_Dword type and value equals 1\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Edge'\n                        : name equals 'InPrivateModeAvailability'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"InPrivate mode must be disabled.","mitigations":"","discussion":"This setting specifies whether the user can open pages in InPrivate mode in Microsoft Edge.\n\nIf this policy is not configured or set it to \"Enabled\", users can open pages in InPrivate mode.\n\nSet this policy to \"Disabled\" to stop users from using InPrivate mode.\n\nSet this policy to \"Forced\" to always use InPrivate mode.\n\nPolicy options mapping:\n- Enabled (0) = InPrivate mode available\n- Disabled (1) = InPrivate mode disabled\n- Forced (2) = InPrivate mode forced","stig_uuid":"88DD52C8-6BF8-1014-BE64-C3AC2D3D7E13","group_id":"V-235723","potential_impacts":"","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-235723","fix_text":"Set the policy value for \"Computer Configuration/Administrative Templates/Microsoft Edge/Configure InPrivate mode availability\" to \"enabled\" and select \"InPrivate mode disabled\".","status":"not_a_finding","uuid":"88E0CFA8-6BF8-1014-9874-ED80B345CFC0","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.edge:def:102","href":"U_MS_Edge_V2R5_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV15-oval.xml"},"rule_id_src":"SV-235723r960864_rule","ia_controls":"","check_content":"The policy value for \"Computer Configuration/Administrative Templates/Microsoft Edge/Configure InPrivate mode availability\" must be set to \"enabled\" with the option value set to \"InPrivate mode disabled\".\n\nUse the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key:\nHKLM\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Edge\n\nIf the value for \"InPrivateModeAvailability\" is not set to \"REG_DWORD = 1\", this is a finding.","rule_id":"SV-235723r960864","mitigation_control":"","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","group_tree":{"id":"V-235723","title":"SRG-APP-000080"},"reference_identifier":"5280","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":"","rule_version":"EDGE-00-000005","severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-APP-000080","ccis":["CCI-000166"]},{"security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Background processing must be disabled.","mitigations":"","discussion":"Background processing allows Microsoft Edge processes to start at OS sign-in and keep running after the last browser window is closed. In this scenario, background apps and the current browsing session remain active, including any session cookies. An open background process displays an icon in the system tray, and can be closed from there.\n\nIf this policy is enabled, background mode is turned on.\n\nIf this policy is disabled, background mode is turned off.\n\nIf this policy is not configured, background mode is initially turned off, and the user can configure its behavior in edge://settings/system.","stig_uuid":"88DD52C8-6BF8-1014-BE64-C3AC2D3D7E13","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:09:53\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Enable the setting 'Continue running background apps after Microsoft Edge closes')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.edge:tst:10300 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Enable the setting 'Continue running background apps after Microsoft Edge closes'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.edge:obj:10300 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Edge'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'BackgroundModeEnabled'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.edge:ste:10 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Reg_Dword type and value equals 0\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Edge'\n                        : name equals 'BackgroundModeEnabled'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","status":"not_a_finding","uuid":"88E0D78F-6BF8-1014-AFFF-BA083AEDFE62","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.edge:def:103","href":"U_MS_Edge_V2R5_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV15-oval.xml"},"potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-235724","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-235724","fix_text":"Set the policy value for \"Computer Configuration/Administrative Templates/Microsoft Edge/Continue running background apps after Microsoft Edge closes\" to \"Disabled\".","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000141","id":"V-235724"},"responsibility":"","reference_identifier":"5280","third_party_tools":"","rule_id_src":"SV-235724r960963_rule","check_content":"The policy value for \"Computer Configuration/Administrative Templates/Microsoft Edge/Continue running background apps after Microsoft Edge closes\" must be set to \"Disabled\".\n\nUse the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key:\nHKLM\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Edge\n\nIf the value for \"BackgroundModeEnabled\" is not set to \"REG_DWORD = 0\", this is a finding.","ia_controls":"","rule_id":"SV-235724r960963","mitigation_control":"","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"rule_version":"EDGE-00-000006"},{"weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","responsibility":"","reference_identifier":"5280","third_party_tools":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-235725","title":"SRG-APP-000141"},"check_content":"The policy value for \"Computer Configuration/Administrative Templates/Microsoft Edge/Content settings/Default pop-up window setting\" must be set to \"Enabled\" with the option value set to \"Do not allow any site to show  pop-ups\".\n\nUse the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key:\nHKLM\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Edge\n\nIf the value for DefaultPopupsSetting is not set to \"REG_DWORD = 2\", this is a finding.","ia_controls":"","rule_id_src":"SV-235725r960963_rule","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-235725r960963","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141","severity":"medium","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"rule_version":"EDGE-00-000008","discussion":"Set whether websites can show pop-up windows. Pop-ups can be allowed on all websites (\"AllowPopups\") or blocked on all sites (\"BlockPopups\").\n\nIf this policy is configured, pop-up windows are blocked by default, and users can change this setting.\n\nPolicy options mapping:\n- AllowPopups (1) = Allow all sites to show pop-ups.\n- BlockPopups (2) = Do not allow any site to show pop-ups.","mitigations":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The ability of sites to show pop-ups must be disabled.","stig_uuid":"88DD52C8-6BF8-1014-BE64-C3AC2D3D7E13","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:09:53\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Do not allow any site to show pop-ups)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.edge:tst:10400 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Do not allow any site to show pop-ups\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.edge:obj:10400 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Edge'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'DefaultPopupsSetting'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.edge:ste:12 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Reg_Dword type and value equals 2\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '2'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Edge'\n                        : name equals 'DefaultPopupsSetting'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '2'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.edge:def:104","href":"U_MS_Edge_V2R5_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV15-oval.xml"},"uuid":"88E0DED0-6BF8-1014-B099-AC148AD969E4","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-235725","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-235725","fix_text":"Set the policy value for \"Computer Configuration/Administrative Templates/Microsoft Edge/Content settings/Default pop-up window setting\" to \"Enabled\" with the option value set to \"Do not allow any site to show  pop-ups\"."},{"security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The default search provider must be set to use an encrypted connection.","mitigations":"","discussion":"Allows a list of list of up to 10 search engines to be configured, one of which must be marked as the default search engine. The encoding does not need to be specified. Starting in Microsoft Edge 80, the suggest_url and image_search_url parameters are optional. The optional parameter, image_search_post_params (consists of comma-separated name/value pairs), is available starting in Microsoft Edge 80.\n\nStarting in Microsoft Edge 83, search engine discovery can be enabled with the allow_search_engine_discovery optional parameter. This parameter must be the first item in the list. If allow_search_engine_discovery is not specified, search engine discovery will be disabled by default. Starting in Microsoft Edge 84, this policy can be set as a recommended policy to allow search provider discovery. The allow_search_engine_discovery optional parameter does not need to be added.\n\nIf this policy is enabled, users cannot add, remove, or change any search engine in the list. Users can set their default search engine to any search engine in the list.\n\nIf this policy is disabled or not configured, users can modify the search engines list as desired.","stig_uuid":"88DD52C8-6BF8-1014-BE64-C3AC2D3D7E13","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:09:53\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (The default search provider URL must be set to perform encrypted searches.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.edge:tst:23572601 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : The default search provider URL must be set to perform encrypted searches.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : No collected item may match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.edge:obj:23572601 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : DefaultSearchProviderSearchURL\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Edge'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'ManagedSearchEngines'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.edge:ste:23572601 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : No search engine may be unencrypted (http://)\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must match the pattern 'http://'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Edge'\n                        : name equals 'ManagedSearchEngines'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_sz'\n                        : value equals '[{\"allow_search_engine_discovery\": false},{\"is_default\": true,\"name\": \"Microsoft Bing\",\"keyword\": \"bing\",\"search_url\": \"https://www.bing.com/search?q={searchTerms}\"},{\"name\": \"Google\",\"keyword\": \"google\",\"search_url\": \"https://www.google.com/search?q={searchTerms}\"}]'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","status":"not_a_finding","uuid":"88E0E650-6BF8-1014-8CCE-F10EA3169544","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Edge_V2R5_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV15-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.edge:def:235726"},"potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-235726","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-235726","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for \"Computer Configuration/Administrative Templates/Microsoft Edge/Manage Search Engines\".","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","group_tree":{"id":"V-235726","title":"SRG-APP-000141"},"responsibility":"","reference_identifier":"5280","third_party_tools":"","rule_id_src":"SV-235726r960963_rule","check_content":"The policy value for \"Computer Configuration/Administrative Templates/Microsoft Edge/Manage Search Engines\" must be configured.\n\nUse the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key:\nHKLM\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Edge\n\nExample REG_SZ value text for \"ManagedSearchEngines\":\n[{\"allow_search_engine_discovery\": false},{\"is_default\": true,\"name\": \"Microsoft Bing\",\"keyword\": \"bing\",\"search_url\": \"https://www.bing.com/search?q={searchTerms}\"},{\"name\": \"Google\",\"keyword\": \"google\",\"search_url\": \"https://www.google.com/search?q={searchTerms}\"}]\n\nIf any of the search URLs in the list do not begin with \"https\", this is a finding.","ia_controls":"","rule_id":"SV-235726r960963","mitigation_control":"","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"rule_version":"EDGE-00-000009"},{"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:09:53\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Disable Microsoft Edge data synchronization)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.edge:tst:10500 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Disable Microsoft Edge data synchronization\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.edge:obj:10500 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Edge'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'SyncDisabled'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.edge:ste:11 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Reg_Dword type and value equals 1\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Edge'\n                        : name equals 'SyncDisabled'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","mitigations":"","discussion":"Disables data synchronization in Microsoft Edge. This policy also prevents the sync consent prompt from appearing.\n\nIf this policy is not set or applied as recommended, users will be able to turn sync on or off. If this policy is applied as mandatory, users will not be able to turn on sync.","rule_title":"Data Synchronization must be disabled.","security_override_guidance":"","stig_uuid":"88DD52C8-6BF8-1014-BE64-C3AC2D3D7E13","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-235727","group_id":"V-235727","potential_impacts":"","fix_text":"Set the policy value for \"Computer Configuration/Administrative Templates/Microsoft Edge/Disable synchronization of data using Microsoft sync services\" to \"Enabled\".","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.edge:def:105","href":"U_MS_Edge_V2R5_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV15-oval.xml"},"uuid":"88E0EDE1-6BF8-1014-8311-A877C070A4BF","rule_id_src":"SV-235727r960963_rule","ia_controls":"","check_content":"The policy value for \"Computer Configuration/Administrative Templates/Microsoft Edge/Disable synchronization of data using Microsoft sync services\" must be set to \"Enabled\".\n\nUse the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key:\nHKLM\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Edge\n\nIf the value for \"SyncDisabled\" is not set to \"REG_DWORD = 1\", this is a finding.","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"rule_id":"SV-235727r960963","mitigation_control":"","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000141","id":"V-235727"},"responsibility":"","reference_identifier":"5280","third_party_tools":"","rule_version":"EDGE-00-000010","severity":"low","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141","ccis":["CCI-000381"]},{"reference_identifier":"5280","third_party_tools":"","responsibility":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000141","id":"V-235728"},"weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-235728r960963","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"check_content":"The policy value for \"Computer Configuration/Administrative Templates/Microsoft Edge/Enable network prediction\" must be set to \"Enabled\" with the option value set to \"Don't predict network actions on any network connection\".\n\nUse the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key:\nHKLM\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Edge\n\nIf the value for NetworkPredictionOptions is not set to \"REG_DWORD = 2\", this is a finding.","ia_controls":"","rule_id_src":"SV-235728r960963_rule","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"group_title":"SRG-APP-000141","severity":"medium","rule_version":"EDGE-00-000011","stig_uuid":"88DD52C8-6BF8-1014-BE64-C3AC2D3D7E13","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Network prediction must be disabled.","discussion":"Enables network prediction and prevents users from changing this setting.\n\nThis controls DNS prefetching, TCP and SSL pre-connection, and pre-rendering of web pages.\n\nIf this policy is not configured, network prediction is enabled but the user can change it.\n\nPolicy options mapping:\n- NetworkPredictionAlways (0) = Predict network actions on any network connection.\n- NetworkPredictionWifiOnly (1) = Not supported; if this value is used it will be treated as if \"Predict network actions on any network connection\" (0) was set.\n- NetworkPredictionNever (2) = Do not predict network actions on any network connection.","mitigations":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:09:53\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Disable network prediction for MS Edge)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.edge:tst:10600 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Disable network prediction for MS Edge\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.edge:obj:10600 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Check the registry value stored at HKLM\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Edge\\NetworkPredictionOptions\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Edge'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'NetworkPredictionOptions'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.edge:ste:12 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Reg_Dword type and value equals 2\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '2'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Edge'\n                        : name equals 'NetworkPredictionOptions'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '2'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","uuid":"88E0F518-6BF8-1014-90D2-D980B8ECA29A","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Edge_V2R5_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV15-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.edge:def:106"},"status":"not_a_finding","fix_text":"Set the policy value for \"Computer Configuration/Administrative Templates/Microsoft Edge/Enable network prediction\" to \"Enabled\" with the option value set to \"Don't predict network actions on any network connection\".","group_id":"V-235728","potential_impacts":"","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-235728"},{"comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-235729r960963","ia_controls":"","check_content":"The policy value for \"Computer Configuration/Administrative Templates/Microsoft Edge/Enable search suggestions\" must be set to \"Disabled\".\n\nUse the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key:\nHKLM\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Edge\n\nIf the value for \"SearchSuggestEnabled\" is not set to \"REG_DWORD = 0\", this is a finding.","rule_id_src":"SV-235729r960963_rule","responsibility":"","reference_identifier":"5280","third_party_tools":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-235729","title":"SRG-APP-000141"},"weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","rule_version":"EDGE-00-000012","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"group_title":"SRG-APP-000141","severity":"medium","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:09:53\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Disable the setting 'Enable search suggestions')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.edge:tst:10700 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Disable the setting 'Enable search suggestions'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.edge:obj:10700 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Edge'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'SearchSuggestEnabled'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.edge:ste:10 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Reg_Dword type and value equals 0\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Edge'\n                        : name equals 'SearchSuggestEnabled'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","stig_uuid":"88DD52C8-6BF8-1014-BE64-C3AC2D3D7E13","discussion":"Enables web search suggestions in the Microsoft Edge Address Bar and Auto-Suggest List, and prevents users from changing this policy.\n\nIf this policy is enabled, web search suggestions are used.\n\nIf this policy is disabled, web search suggestions are never used; however, local history and local favorites suggestions still appear. If this policy is disabled, neither the typed characters nor the URLs visited will be included in telemetry to Microsoft.\n\nIf this policy is not set, search suggestions are enabled but the user can change that.","mitigations":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Search suggestions must be disabled.","fix_text":"Set the policy value for \"Computer Configuration/Administrative Templates/Microsoft Edge/Enable search suggestions\" to \"Disabled\".","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-235729","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-235729","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.edge:def:107","href":"U_MS_Edge_V2R5_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV15-oval.xml"},"uuid":"88E0FC8E-6BF8-1014-A266-B7EF3FD092E4","status":"not_a_finding"},{"responsibility":"","reference_identifier":"5280","third_party_tools":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000141","id":"V-235730"},"weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-235730r960963","ia_controls":"","check_content":"The policy value for \"Computer Configuration/Administrative Templates/Microsoft Edge/Allow importing of autofill form data\" must be set to \"disabled\".\n\nUse the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key:\nHKLM\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Edge\n\nIf the value for \"ImportAutofillFormData\" is not set to \"REG_DWORD = 0\", this is a finding.","rule_id_src":"SV-235730r960963_rule","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"group_title":"SRG-APP-000141","severity":"medium","rule_version":"EDGE-00-000013","stig_uuid":"88DD52C8-6BF8-1014-BE64-C3AC2D3D7E13","discussion":"Allows users to import autofill form data from another browser into Microsoft Edge.\n\nIf this policy is enabled, the option to manually import autofill data is automatically selected.\n\nIf this policy is disabled, autofill form data is not imported at first run, and users cannot import it manually.\n\nIf this policy is not configured, autofill data is imported at first run, and users can choose whether to import this data manually during later browsing sessions.\n\nThis policy cannot be set as a recommendation. This means that Microsoft Edge will import autofill data on first run, but users can select or clear autofill data option during manual import.","mitigations":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Importing of autofill form data must be disabled.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:09:53\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Disable importing of autofill form data)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.edge:tst:10800 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\n