discussion":"Allows users to import browser settings from another browser into Microsoft Edge.\n\nIf this policy is enabled, the Browser settings check box is automatically selected in the Import browser data dialog box.\n\nIf this policy is disabled, browser settings are not imported at first run, and users cannot import them manually.\n\nIf this policy is not configured, browser settings are imported at first run, and users can choose whether to import them manually during later browsing sessions.","stig_uuid":"88DD52C8-6BF8-1014-BE64-C3AC2D3D7E13","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:09:53\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Disable importing of autofill form data)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.edge:tst:10900 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Disable importing of autofill form data\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.edge:obj:10900 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Edge'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'ImportBrowserSettings'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.edge:ste:10 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Reg_Dword type and value equals 0\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n 